Now that China is increasingly active in the use of artificial intelligence, the United States should double the resources it spends on research in that field, says the inventor and artificial intelligence user Kai-Fu Lee who has worked at Google, Microsoft and Apple.
The remarks were said after different departments of the U.S. government issued announcements of artificial intelligence, even though the U.S. has no formal overall plan for artificial intelligence.
China, however, announced its plan last year: it aims to be in first place in innovation with artificial intelligence by 2030.
"It would be a good start to double the funding, which goes into artificial intelligence research, considering that all the other countries are so much further behind the United States, and we're waiting to see the next big discovery in the field of artificial intelligence," Lee said.
