He worked at Carnegie Mellon at Carnegie Mellon University, which won the best U.S. player in Othello, and later served as managing director at Microsoft Research and the president of the Chinese department at Google.
Lee talked about previous technical competitions, which were held by U.S. authorities, such as the Defense Department's robotic competition, and asked when the next competition would be held, to spot the next pioneers.
Scientists in the U.S
"It's not China's biggest thinkers, it's the companies," Lee said.
Facebook, Google and other technology companies have recruited geniuses from universities to work on artificial intelligence in recent years.
