"I think those who have a doctorate in artificial intelligence should be granted a residence permit automatically," he said.
China's parliament issued its future artificial intelligence plan in July 2017.
China's Institute of Natural Sciences provides funds to people who work at university institutions, similar to the National Science Foundation and similar public institutions do in the United States, but the quality of scientific work is worse in China, Lee said.
