The latest news of algae blooms: Concentration decreases in Pinellas, Manatee and Sarasota
The latest news from the Florida Fish and Wildlife Commission shows a general reduction in algae blooms in parts of the Tampa Bay area.
According to FWC, more worn-out algae blooms are reported in certain areas of Pinellas, Manatee, Sarasota Charlotte and Collier counties - indicating decreasing concentrations.
Algae bloom extends over a 200-kilometre coastline from northern Pinellas to the southern part of the Lee counties.
You can find unique flowers about 16 kilometers from Hillsborough County, but in fewer places compared to last week.
Algae blooms have also been reported in Pasco County.
Moderate concentrations in or near Pinellas County were reported last week, low to high concentrations off the shores of Hillsborough county, very low to high concentrations in Manatee County, very low to high concentrations in or around Sarasota county, extremely low to moderate concentrations in Charlotte County, extremely low to high concentrations in or off the coasts of Lee County and low concentrations in Collier County.
Irritation in the respiratory system in Pinellas, Manatee, Sarasota, Lee and Collier counties is still reported.
There were no reports of respiratory irritation in northwestern Florida over last week.
